<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">Banat Republic</h1><p class="st-meta">1918 CE – 1918 CE · capital Temesvár</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Short-lived multi-ethnic republic proclaimed in Temesvár in 1918, an attempt to keep the mixed Banat region together as Austria-Hungary collapsed.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>As <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austria-Hungary</a> dissolved at the end of October 1918, Social Democrats and local leaders in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timisoara">Temesvár</a>, led by the lawyer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otto-roth">Otto Roth</a>, proclaimed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banat">Banat</a> Republic on 1 November 1918. They hoped to preserve the unity of the Banat, home to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romanians">Romanians</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbs">Serbs</a>, Germans, Hungarians and others, within a democratic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>A people's council with representatives of the different nationalities tried to keep order, organise a civic guard and supply the towns. The republic had little military force and was not recognised by any state; Romanian and Serbian national councils in the region rejected it.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Serbian troops entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timisoara">Temesvár</a> on 15 November 1918 and ended the republic within about two weeks of its proclamation. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banat">Banat</a> was later divided between <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-romania">Romania</a>, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-yugoslavia">Kingdom of Yugoslavia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> by the post-war treaties of 1919 to 1920.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/banat-republic.jpg" alt="Banat Republic" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: User:R-41 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Socialist_red_flag.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1918 CE – 1918 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Temesvár</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Otto Roth</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic and Orthodox Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>German, Hungarian, Romanian, Serbian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/romania">Romania</a>, <a href="/countries/serbia">Serbia</a>, <a href="/countries/hungary">Hungary</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Republic of Banat</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1918&amp;focus=banat-republic" aria-label="Banat Republic on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5183 565 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Banat Republic lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5503 821L5445 768M5503 821L5488 850"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5445 768h0M5488 850h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5503 821h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5503 821h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1918&amp;focus=banat-republic">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
